o damaged sales, he added. Is your local TG Jones store closing its doors? Let us know in the comments. Share

Share PureGym is planning to open around 60 new sites worldwide in 2026. The Leeds-headquartered fitness chain says it also aims to accelerate its global expansion over the second half of 2026, with long-term ambitions for more than 750 additional locations worldwide. Of the 17 new gyms opened over the first half, 15 were in the UK. PureGym has sites in St Ives, St Neots, Peterborough and Wisbech. The company currently operates 728 sites, including 467 in the UK, 128 in Denmark, 49 in Switzerland, and 61 in the US, as well as having a franchise agreement in Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates.  A post shared by PureGym (@puregymofficial)  Alex Wood, chief executive of PureGym, said: "The long-term fundamentals of our sector remain extremely attractive. "Consumers are placing ever greater importance on their health and wellbeing, while the increasing availability of convenient and affordable gyms is bringing more people into fitness." The group is also expanding its dedicated women’s workout areas, which are now available in 73 UK gyms. An additional 20 spaces were introduced in the six months to the end of June. These facilities have been rolled out over the past couple of years, with expansion accelerating due to what the company describes as a “positive reception to these dedicated training spaces designed to boost female members’ comfort and confidence.” PureGym reported a 23 per cent rise in underlying earnings to £123.6 million for the six months to June 30. (function (d, s, n) {
